+(** Validate an original byte-valued alignment request and return its
+    effective contribution. Reject negative, non-power-of-two, GNU zero and
+    values greater than 2^32 with [Kernel.abort]. C11 zero yields [None].
+    With the private Clang policy, an unsigned-32 bit-cache contribution of
+    zero also yields [None]; it is not an object's natural alignment.
+    This helper does not alter source expressions or attributes. *)
+val effectiveAlignment: c11:bool -> Z.t -> int option
+
+(** Read a literal alignment parameter or fold a typed sizeof/alignof query.
+    Returns [None] for arithmetic and other forms whose target C integer
+    kinds have been lost by conversion to attribute parameters. Recursive
+    queries are not silently interpreted with ignored alignment attributes.
+    This is deliberately narrower than {!intOfAttrparam}. *)
+val integerOfAlignmentAttrparam: attrparam -> Z.t option
